From: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: keep -Wmissing-prototypes from breaking the build

The SSDK sources are full of non-static helpers that are exported through
tables without prototypes.  Toolchains newer than the one QSDK is built
with enable -Wmissing-prototypes/-Wmissing-declarations by default, which
-Werror then turns into a hard error.  Disable those two warnings.

Signed-off-by: Qianzf <qianzf@example.com>
---
--- a/mk/cflags.mk	2026-07-20 11:22:55.000000000 +0800
+++ b/mk/cflags.mk	2026-11-21 10:38:47.133246048 +0800
@@ -499,4 +499,4 @@
 #############################################
 #            combine all cflags
 #############################################
-ccflags-y += ${MODULE_INC} ${MODULE_CFLAG} -DFALLTHROUGH -Werror -Wall
+ccflags-y += ${MODULE_INC} ${MODULE_CFLAG} -DFALLTHROUGH -Werror -Wall -Wno-missing-prototypes -Wno-missing-declarations
